    "auditExceptionNotes": {
      "GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj": "sharp <0.35.0 (libvips CVEs). Accepted risk: sharp 0.35.x crashes on the Vercel Lambda runtime (newsletter thumbnails returned HTTP 500, verified), so the upgrade is not deployable. Exposure is bounded: sharp only ever processes images fetched through lib/security/safe-image-fetch.ts, which enforces an exact-hostname allowlist (own Blob store + own Supabase project), an 8 MiB byte cap, a 16 MP pixel cap and PNG/JPEG/WebP magic-byte validation - so untrusted images never reach libvips. Owner: Mattes. Re-evaluate when sharp ships a release that runs on Vercel Lambda, or at the latest on 2026-11-02.",
      "GHSA-jmr9-qjv8-65gv": "extract-zip <=2.0.1 (unvalidated symlink path traversal). Accepted risk: NO patched version exists - 2.0.1 is the latest published release and the advisory lists patched_versions '<0.0.0', so an override cannot fix it. Reaches us transitively via @remotion/renderer (also through @remotion/bundler, @remotion/studio, @remotion/lambda), the video-rendering chain. Exposure is bounded: Remotion uses extract-zip to unpack its own browser downloads, never archives from user input, and no endpoint of this app accepts ZIP uploads - exploiting it would require control over the Remotion download itself, at which point the supply chain is already compromised. Owner: Mattes. Re-evaluate when extract-zip ships a release beyond 2.0.1 (npm view extract-zip version) or Remotion switches unpacking libraries, at the latest on 2026-11-24."
    }
